    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0491" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/4237: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-27T13:00:00+02:00">June 27, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 28—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>302. The Bolshevik Government presented at 10 o’clock last night a 24-hour
                    ultimatum to the Rumanian Government demanding the immediate return of
                    Bessarabia and that part of Bukowina inhabited by Ukrainians as indicated on a
                    map yet to reach Bucharest. The preamble of the ultimatum refers to Bessarabia
                    having been taken at a time when Russia was militarily weak “an unfortunate
                    state of <pb facs="0492" n="480" xml:id="pg480"/> affairs which now no longer
                        exists.”<anchor n="38" xml:id="d501-f1"/> In my personal opinion this
                    ultimatum will be rejected.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d501-f1" n="38" xml:id="d501-f1-content">
                <p>The Rumanian invasion of Bessarabia began in January 1918, and with the
                    disintegration of Russia after the Bolshevik revolution the province became
                    effectively Rumanian. A treaty signed at Paris on October 28, 1920, between
                    Great Britain, France, Italy, Japan, and Rumania, formally assenting to the
                    acquisition of Bessarabia by Rumania, was never ratified by Japan and was not
                    actually in force; for draft and correspondence regarding the treaty, see <ref
                        target="frus1920v03#pg_426">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1920, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi> pp. 426</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1920v03#pg_435">435</ref>; for text, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >British and Foreign State Papers</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >cxiii</hi>, p. 647. The United States was not party to this treaty and for
                    a long time refused to recognize Rumanian sovereignty over Bessarabia, until <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> recognition was granted in 1933; see <ref
                        target="frus1930v03#pg_801">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1930, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 801</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1930v03#pg_807">807</ref>; <ref target="frus1932v02#pg_503">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1932, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, pp. 503</ref>–<ref target="frus1932v02#pg_508">508</ref>; and
                        <ref target="frus1933v02#pg_656">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, 1933, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, pp. 656</ref>–<ref target="frus1933v02#pg_682">682</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
